#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:3
msgid "Expose apps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:5
msgid ""
"Control which apps, manual pages, and shell completions an environment links "
"onto your ``PATH``, without rebuilding it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:10
msgid "Hide an app"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:12
msgid ""
"Use ``unexpose`` when another command with the same name should win, but you "
"want to keep the environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:14
msgid "$ pipx unexpose ansible"
msgstr "$ pipx unexpose ansible"

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:18
msgid ""
"pipx removes the apps, manual pages, and shell completions recorded for that "
"environment from its global directories. Upgrade and reinstall keep it "
"hidden, and injected apps stay hidden too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:23
msgid "Restore an app"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:25
msgid "$ pipx expose ansible"
msgstr "$ pipx expose ansible"

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:29
msgid ""
"pipx links each recorded app, manual page, and shell completion that is "
"missing from its target directory, without rebuilding the environment. Run "
"it on an exposed environment to restore a link you deleted. When a file pipx "
"does not own already sits at a target path, pipx leaves it in place, links "
"the rest, and exits with ``1``. Move that file away and run ``pipx expose`` "
"again to link the skipped resource."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:36
msgid "Expose a dependency's apps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:38
msgid ""
"A dependency's apps are not exposed by default. Select them at install time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:40
msgid "``--include-deps`` exposes apps and manual pages from every dependency:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:42
msgid "$ pipx install nox --include-deps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:46
msgid ""
"``--include-resources-from PACKAGE`` exposes resources from one dependency; "
"repeat it to select more:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:48
msgid "$ pipx install \"nox[tox_to_nox]\" --include-resources-from tox"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:52
msgid ""
"pipx records the selection so upgrade and reinstall preserve it. The install "
"fails and rolls back when a selected package is not a dependency that ships "
"apps, manual pages, or shell completions. Both options also work on ``pipx "
"inject``; see :doc:`inject-packages`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:58
msgid ""
"``--include-apps-from`` was renamed to ``--include-resources-from``. pipx "
"still reads the old name from metadata written by earlier versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:63
msgid "Verify it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:65
msgid "$ pipx list"
msgstr "$ pipx list"

#: ../../../how-to/expose-apps.rst:69
msgid ""
"The exposed apps appear under their environment. Run one to confirm it "
"resolves on your ``PATH``."
msgstr ""
